  "body_html": "<h1>Residual Moment-Map Condition for Epipelagic Data</h1>\n<p>Let \\((x,\\lambda,\\chi)\\) and \\((x',\\lambda',\\chi')\\) be epipelagic data of the same order \\(m\\) for \\(G\\) and \\(G'\\). Let \\(L_x\\) and \\(L_{x'}\\) be the corresponding self-dual lattice functions, set \\(B=L_x\\otimes L_{x'}\\), and define\n\\[\nX=B_{-1/(2m)}/B_{-1/(2m)+}.\n\\]</p>\n<p>The residual moment-map condition is the existence of \\(\\bar w\\in X\\) such that\n\\[\n\\lambda=M_{-1/(2m)}(\\bar w),\\qquad\n\\lambda'=-M'_{-1/(2m)}(\\bar w).\n\\]\nIt is the geometric condition that the two epipelagic minimal \\(K\\)-type functionals arise from the same residual oscillator-model vector.</p>",
  "proof_html": null,
